WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.989
Is mathematics invented

00:00:01.800 --> 00:00:02.802
or discovered

00:00:03.342 --> 00:00:04.426
A long Abakcus

00:00:04.250 --> 00:00:05.346
essay that uses

00:00:05.158 --> 00:00:06.325
Euclid's proof that

00:00:06.137 --> 00:00:07.162
the primes never

00:00:06.974 --> 00:00:07.799
end to ask

00:00:07.611 --> 00:00:08.695
whether mathematical

00:00:08.507 --> 00:00:10.240
truths exist before

00:00:10.193 --> 00:00:11.396
anyone proves them

00:00:11.926 --> 00:00:12.798
The proof has

00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:13.989
never needed correction

00:00:13.884 --> 00:00:14.791
which raises the

00:00:14.603 --> 00:00:15.227
puzzle

00:00:15.358 --> 00:00:16.584
if mathematics is

00:00:16.395 --> 00:00:17.633
invented like chess

00:00:17.751 --> 00:00:18.388
it should be

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:19.201
ours to change

00:00:19.367 --> 00:00:19.992
and if it

00:00:19.803 --> 00:00:20.841
is discovered like

00:00:20.652 --> 00:00:21.477
a continent

00:00:21.714 --> 00:00:22.279
we owe an

00:00:22.091 --> 00:00:23.117
account of where

00:00:22.928 --> 00:00:23.777
it was before

00:00:23.589 --> 00:00:24.131
us

00:00:24.662 --> 00:00:26.395
Sometime around 300

00:00:26.207 --> 00:00:27.963
BC in Alexandria

00:00:28.129 --> 00:00:29.036
a teacher named

00:00:28.848 --> 00:00:29.933
Euclid wrote down

00:00:29.745 --> 00:00:30.770
an argument that

00:00:30.594 --> 00:00:31.253
fits on the

00:00:31.065 --> 00:00:31.808
back of an

00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:32.327
envelope

00:00:32.862 --> 00:00:33.876
Full story on

00:00:33.687 --> 00:00:34.583
the dashboard
